{
 "modules": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "EMOTION\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 7, CC 97 to 112\n   1 Strength of the feeling\n   2 How they move\n   3 Feeling in the voice\n   4 Amount of movement\n   5 Amount said\n   6 Posture changes\n   7 Size of the actions\n   8 Mood of the place\n   9 Mood of the light\n  10 Against the last scene\n  11 Feeling gap between characters\n  12 Mixed feelings\n  13 Said against meant\n  14 The eyes\n  15 The hands\n  16 Personal space\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 8, CC 1 to 16\n   1 Release\n   2 What the audience feels\n   3 suite: Feels loving\n   4 suite: Feels joyful\n   5 suite: Feels curious\n   6 suite: Feels melancholy\n   7 suite: Feels anxious\n   8 suite: Feels fearful\n   9 suite: Feels angry\n  10 suite: Feels triumphant\n  11 suite: Feels absurd\n  12 suite: Feels dreamlike\n  13 suite: Emotion lens\n  14 suite: Feeling of the scene\n  15 suite: Held-back tears\n  16 suite: Rage boils over\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 8, CC 17 to 32\n   1 suite: Quiet joy\n   2 suite: Frozen fear\n   3 suite: Mood whiplash\n   4 suite: Calm in the storm\n   5 suite: The mask slips\n   6 suite: Laughing through tears\n   7 suite: Brave face\n   8 suite: Dawning realization\n   9 suite: The breakdown\n  10 suite: Cold fury\n  11 suite: Giddy relief\n  12 suite: Numb shock\n  13 suite: Awkward tenderness\n  14 suite: Dread: we know, they don't\n  15 suite: Cartoon feelings\n  16 pair: When the mood of the light drops, the strength of the feeling rises\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 8, CC 33 to 48\n   1 pair: When the feeling grows stronger, the posture changes more often\n   2 pair: When a scene feels the opposite of the last one, the color shifts too\n   3 pair: When a feeling rises, the face shows it before the words\n   4 pair: When anger rises, the voice gets louder\n   5 pair: When fear rises, movement stops\n   6 pair: When one character's feeling overflows, others catch it\n   7 pair: When joy rises, the light warms\n   8 pair: When a trigger appears, the feeling turns\n   9 pair: After a release, the character is lighter\n  10 pair: When said and meant pull apart, the pauses grow\n  11 pair: When people move closer, the feeling grows\n  12 pair: When tears well, the shot gets closer\n  13 pair: When we know more than they do, tension rises\n  14 pair: When feelings mix, the face flickers\n  15 pair: When someone feels loving, hearts pop onto their face\n  16 pair: When someone is joyful, a sun pops onto their face\nCV-CC 5: MIDI channel 8, CC 49 to 64\n   1 pair: When someone turns sad, tears are drawn on\n   2 pair: When someone is anxious, they blush\n   3 pair: When someone is scared, their soul leaves their body\n   4 pair: When someone gets curious, a light bulb pops on\n   5 pair: When someone triumphs, shades pop on\n   6 pair: When things turn absurd, question marks pop on\n   7 pair: When tears are drawn on, the feeling drops\n   8 pair: When a sun pops onto a face, the feeling lifts\n   9 pair: When steam pops on, the feeling winds up\n  10 pair: When a face crackles, the feeling winds up\n  11 pair: When someone laughs till they cry, the audience laughs more\n  12 pair: When the mallet bonks, the feeling turns absurd\n  13 pair: When the room feels cozy, people sit closer\n  14 pair: When the voice breaks, the tears come\n  15 pair: When the hands clench, a bigger action follows\n  16 pair: When the actions get bigger, the voice gives way\nCV-CC 6: MIDI channel 8, CC 65 to 72\n   1 pair: When someone freezes, a slow-burn reaction follows\n   2 pairs: The body tells first\n   3 pairs: Feelings spread\n   4 pairs: What isn't said\n   5 pairs: Closeness and dread\n   6 pairs: The face tells the feeling\n   7 pairs: The mood moves the feeling\n   8 pairs: Holding it in, until"
   },
   "pos": [
